---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="HeaderCheck Support"
  description="Support for HeaderCheck: how to get headers, Pro features, and how to contact Nick."
>
  <section class="mast">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kicker">HeaderCheck</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Quick help for the on-device email authentication analyzer.
      </p>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What HeaderCheck does</h2>
        <p>
          HeaderCheck shows plain-language SPF, DKIM, and DMARC verdicts from
          pasted headers or an .eml file. Everything runs on your iPhone or
          iPad. There is no account and no upload to a developer server.
        </p>

        <h2>How to get headers on iPhone</h2>
        <p>
          Apple Mail does not show raw headers in a convenient copy field. A
          reliable path is to forward the message as an attachment (or use Share
          / Open In) and open the .eml in HeaderCheck. In Gmail or iCloud on the
          web, use Show original / view message source, then paste into the App.
          The in-app Learn tab walks through these steps.
        </p>

        <h2>Free and Pro</h2>
        <p>
          Paste and core verdicts are available on the free tier. HeaderCheck
          Pro is a one-time purchase that unlocks PDF export, analysis history
          beyond the free cap, and .eml import. Purchases are handled by Apple.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Email{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=HeaderCheck%20Support`}>
            {site.email}
          </a>{" "}
          with the device model, iOS version, and a short description of the
          issue. Do not send full email headers or message contents unless you
          intentionally want help reviewing a specific sample.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          See the{" "}
          <a href="/headercheck/privacy">HeaderCheck Privacy Policy</a> for how
          data is handled.
        </p>

        <p class="back">
          <a href="/headercheck">Back to HeaderCheck</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .mast {
    padding: 4.5rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem);
  }

  .lede {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    max-width: 36rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .prose {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #d1d5db;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 1.7rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .back {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
